-- title:
--   A k₀-form F₀ of the full-level function field
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a valuation subring with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ evaluating into $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$). Assume the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ of the full level-$M'$ field lies inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change of the $X_H$-field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$. Given: a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, compatible with coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$; an index $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{F}_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: the explicit quotient-of-integral-Laurent-series description of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, transitivity of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ on the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ together with injectivity and permutation of that family, $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)\cap\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=A$, a regularity-and-specialisation compatibility of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $R_0$ at the place $s$ for functions regular where $j$ is, $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$-invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and existence in each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ of an element $t$ with $t-a$ a unit for all $a\in A$; a regular prolongation $R$ with $R.\mathrm{integers}=O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ and the matching $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}\iff f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$; an element $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$; a subfield $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0\cap A$ such that $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, every element of $A$ being congruent modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$; and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$, $\ell\nmid M'$, a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\zeta_0\in k_0$ and $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$. Then, for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ induced through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, there is an intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ such that: the $k_0$-subfield generated by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$; $F_0$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, any $c_1,\dots,c_m\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and any $a_1,\dots,a_m$ in the join of $k_0(K')$ and $F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ force all $a_i=0$; and every element of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients, i.e. lies in the image of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   This produces a $k_0$-rational form $F_0$ of the full-level function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$ which is a compositum complement of the constants, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, regular over $k_0$ in the linear-disjointness sense, and large enough to contain all functions with rational $q$-expansion, in particular $j$ and its level-$M'$ companion. It is used in the construction of the Igusa base model with prescribed smooth-point stalks, where $j$ must be available inside the level field; the commutation of arithmetic Galois action with the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}$ is the one project ingredient invoked.
-- source:
